-DATASET CSV empty
--

-CASE DijkstraWeightedChain
-LOAD_DYNAMIC_EXTENSION algo
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64 PRIMARY KEY)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE E(FROM N TO N, weight DOUBLE)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id:0}),(:N {id:1}),(:N {id:2})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:N {id:0}),(y:N {id:1}) CREATE (x)-[:E {weight:1}]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:N {id:1}),(y:N {id:2}) CREATE (x)-[:E {weight:3}]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CALL PROJECT_GRAPH('G', ['N'], ['E'])
---- ok
-STATEMENT CALL dijkstra('G', 0) RETURN node.id, distance ORDER BY node.id
---- 3
0|0.000000
1|1.000000
2|4.000000

-CASE DijkstraNegativeWeight
-LOAD_DYNAMIC_EXTENSION algo
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE T(id INT64 PRIMARY KEY)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE R(FROM T TO T, weight DOUBLE)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:T {id:0}),(:T {id:1}),(:T {id:2})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:T {id:0}),(y:T {id:1}) CREATE (x)-[:R {weight:-1}]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:T {id:1}),(y:T {id:2}) CREATE (x)-[:R {weight:2}]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CALL PROJECT_GRAPH('G2', ['T'], ['R'])
---- ok
-STATEMENT CALL dijkstra('G2', 0) RETURN node.id, distance ORDER BY node.id
---- error
Binder exception: DIJKSTRA does not support negative edge weights/capacities.
